{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_m25kxjkyhdx7nxwz5x2fchp6phiyjcdisyzpqovcitlrszvy5d2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Summary of the implementation:\n\n**`src/ulid.rs`** — Implements `ulidgen_r`:\n- Encodes a 48-bit millisecond Unix timestamp into the first 10 chars using Crockford base32 (`0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ`)\n- If the timestamp is identical to the previous call, increments the random portion in place (with carry) and replaces the lowest non-`Z` char with the next alphabet char\n- If overflow occurs, sleeps ~1.23ms and recurses\n- Otherwise fills 16 random bytes via `rand::thread_rng()` and maps each byte mod 32 to a base32 char\n\n**`src/ulidgen.rs`** — Implements the CLI:\n- Parses `-n N` (count) and `-t` (tag-mode) flags\n- In tag mode, reads stdin lines and prefixes each with a fresh ULID\n- Otherwise generates `N` ULIDs to stdout\n\n**`Cargo.toml`** — Added `rand = \"0.8\"` dependency for entropy.\n\nThe 4 tests in `test.rs` (length, structure, uniqueness, sortability) and the placeholder test in `ulid_test.rs` all pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":25022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1053,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8410bbba-2f28-4086-9d8e-3f0d228141d1","uuid":"c3e4c6bd-e347-4abb-b1b6-277726132595"}
